explanation:
The definition applies `Scheme.Cover.mkOfCovers` with these inputs:
- the index type `Φ.cones`;
- the charts `Φ.affineToricChart σ`, the affine toric schemes of the cones;
- the maps `Φ.affineToricChartι σ`, which are the colimit inclusions into `Φ.algebraicRealization`.

The library proves that each of these maps is an open immersion (instance `isOpenImmersion_affineToricChartι`). It also proves that together they cover the scheme (`exists_affineToricChartι_apply_eq`). So this is exactly the textbook cover of X_Σ by the U_σ. The file also checks the expected behaviour on overlaps: the chart of σ meets the chart of τ in the chart of σ ∩ τ.

On generality, the fan is taken over a lattice map N →+ V into a real vector space, which is the standard setting. Mathlib has no toric varieties, so there is no more general version this should have reused.
